  "Question": "A starts traveling at 4 km/h. After 2 hours, B starts from the same place in the same direction at 6 km/h. How many hours after B starts will B catch up with A? (Unit: hours)",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "4",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "For this catch-up problem, let B catch up with A \\(t\\) hours after B starts. Then \\(6t=4(t+2)\\). Solving gives \\(t=4\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Closing the head start\n\nWhen B starts, A is \\(4\\times2=8\\) km ahead. Each hour, B travels \\(6-4=2\\) km farther than A, so the gap shrinks by \\(2\\) km. It therefore takes \\(8\\div2=4\\) hours after B starts to close the gap.",
